					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-macleod" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1922529); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1922529&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973900" alt="Agent MacLeod" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1922529)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/agent-macleod" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1922529); return false;" >Agent MacLeod</a></span> <span class="odate time_1419804128 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Dec 2014 22:02</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2190831">
									

<p>You speak about the status of Directors and their low birthrates, and yet you have nothing to say of the lowly D-Class and Agents. Did you know that the majority of D-Class don't survive past their first month of adulthood, rarely finding mates in that time? And Agents spend most of their time seeking medals, their primary source of sustenance. With the scarcity of medals, Agents almost never have time to reproduce. I've even heard that the Foundation has had to implement an artificial breeding program to keep these two parts of their ecosystem from going extinct. Surely, the Foundation is an ecosystem in danger of disappearing from this world forever.</p>

							</div>

								
					
