														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2192298">
									

<p>Lemme tell you, the contents of that campaign could be a tale series in and of itself and would include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Bumbling, good-hearted and severely put-upon drow deliverywoman quest-giver.</li>
<li>Elf dudes now dress like they're from JoJo's Bizarre Adventure. The typical greeting is flexing and poses, followed by an incredibly firm handshake.</li>
<li>Drugs that make you hallucinate that gnomes are eating your hands.</li>
<li>A talking goat who is also a cleric.</li>
<li>Crashed modron spaceships inhabited by someone's crazy aunt, who is also a mad scientist.</li>
<li>A 455-style boat haunted by the ghosts of people who got mind-flayed.</li>
<li>Inheriting a baby space station made out of meat by helping the father get rid of his psycho stalker girlfriend.</li>
<li>A giant moth caterpillar that emanated psychic barbershop quartet songs.</li>
<li>The culmination of the campaign involved successfully marrying a marilith, luring it into a false sense of security, and then shanking the ever loving shit out of it.</li>
</ul>
<p>Only one of these has not actually happened in a game I've been in / run in real life.</p>

